+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Stock is currently read and mutated inconsistently across carts, checkout, orders, and product responses. This allows overselling, decrements the wrong inventory, fails to restore canceled orders, and reports out-of-stock products as purchasable.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Make the product quantity exposed by `GET /api/v2/product/{sku}` the single stock value used by cart, checkout, cancellation, and availability behavior.
+- Validate cart additions and quantity changes against stock, returning HTTP 409 without partial updates when a requested state is invalid.
+- Validate checkout carts atomically, decrementing exactly each ordered product quantity and refusing insufficient stock with HTTP 409.
+- Restore each canceled order's quantities exactly once and reject transitions away from CANCELED with HTTP 409.
+- Derive storefront `available` and `canBePurchased` from stock while preserving merchant-controlled unavailability.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `stock-consistency`: Enforces one consistent stock value across cart, checkout, order cancellation, and product availability flows.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+- None.
+
+## Impact
+
+The cart and order REST APIs, shopping cart and order facades/services, product/inventory mapping, persistence transaction boundaries, and integration tests are affected. No endpoint paths change; new conflict cases use HTTP 409.
